   "about": "Sets out the legal organization, duties, staffing, and membership of Japan’s Board and Commission of Tourist Industry.",
   "summary": "The enclosure reproduces the April 1930 imperial ordinance establishing the Board of Tourist Industry under the Minister for Railways and the regulations dividing it into Controlling and Investigating and Promoting departments. The departments were responsible for industry guidance, statistics, overseas advertising, tourist sites, hotels, and guides. A July 1930 ordinance establishes the Commission of Tourist Industry, defines its advisory authority and staffing, and provides for as many as sixty commissioners. The concluding page names Tasuku Egi as president, Shuzo Aoki as both commissioner and general secretary, and lists the other commissioners and secretaries.",
